course: dictionary
lesson: 4843
title: Power from moving water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hydroelectric station makes electricity from moving water. Hydro means water and electric means electricity, so hydroelectric means electricity made by water.
explain: Here is how it works. «A hydroelectric dam lets water from a lake rush down through turbines.» The falling water spins the turbines, and the turbines turn generators that make electricity.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence: rush down and turbines matter most. Turbines are big wheels that spin when water pushes on them. Swap in your meaning, "a dam that makes electricity from water", and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some stations are clever. «Some stations pump water uphill at night and let it run down later, like a giant battery.» They store energy when there is spare power, then let the water run down to make electricity when people need more.
fact: Hydro means water, and electric means electricity.
fact: A hydroelectric dam holds water back in a lake, then lets it fall through turbines.
fact: Hydroelectric power is renewable, because the water keeps coming back from rain and rivers.
fact: The Hoover Dam in the USA and the Three Gorges Dam in China are famous hydroelectric dams.
fact: Hydroelectric schemes are clean and steady, but flooded valleys and harm to fish are problems too.
exercise: «A hydroelectric dam lets water from a lake rush down through turbines.» What does hydroelectric mean? | A lake with fish in it | *Making electricity from moving water | Water that is very hot | Making water from electricity
exercise: What do turbines do in a hydroelectric station? | They make the water warmer | They store rain in tanks | *They spin when water pushes on them, which makes electricity | They are dams that hold back lakes
exercise: Which of these is a famous hydroelectric dam? | The Great Wall | *The Hoover Dam in the USA | Big Ben | The Eiffel Tower
test: Why is hydroelectric power called renewable? | *Because the water keeps coming back from rain and rivers | Because it uses coal | Because it is very expensive
test: «Some stations pump water uphill at night and let it run down later, like a giant battery.» What does this tell you? | Batteries make water | Stations never make power | Water runs uphill all day | *Such stations can store energy and use it later
exam: Which is a real con of hydroelectric schemes? | They make no electricity | *Flooded valleys and harm to fish | They are too small to see | Water is never clean
